<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk reopens after closing Sunday.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk reopens after closing Sunday.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's main Black Sea port of Novorossiisk, closed since Sunday night due to bad weather, reopened early on Wednesday, shipping sources said.</p>
<p>The port opened at 0630 local, allowing one crude tanker to berth. A second was due to berth later, the sources said.</p>
<p>Three more crude tankers and a fuel oil tanker were at anchor, with another vessel due to arrive later on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Bad weather and maintenance on a pipeline feeding the port has caused a backlog at Novorossiisk, traders said.</p>
<p>No delays were reported at other Russian ports.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
